# MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT: DIGITAL CORPS HUB LEARNING ACADEMY

## PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Upgrade the existing Digital Corps Hub application by developing a complete, structured, category-based Learning Academy.

The Learning Academy must contain six fully developed digital skills courses. Each course must align directly with its corresponding Digital Skills Quiz category and the knowledge tested by the questions in that category.

This is an extension of the existing application, NOT a new application.

**Do not rebuild the application, replace existing features, discard existing Firebase data, or break existing functionality.**

The goal is to transform the existing "Get a Recommended Learning Track" feature into a proper learning management system (LMS).

---

# PART 1: INSPECT THE EXISTING APPLICATION

Before writing or changing code:

1. Inspect the existing React, TypeScript and Vite application.
2. Inspect the current Firebase configuration and Firestore collections.
3. Identify the existing Digital Skills Quiz implementation.
4. Inspect all six quiz categories and their question banks.
5. Identify how questions, correct answers, explanations, scores and quiz attempts are currently stored.
6. Inspect the existing "Get a Recommended Learning Track" functionality.
7. Inspect the user registration, authentication, participant profile and Admin Portal.
8. Identify existing UI components and reusable layouts.

Create an implementation plan before modifying the application.

Reuse existing collections and components wherever possible. Do not create duplicate collections or replace working systems unnecessarily.

---

# PART 2: THE SIX COMPLETE LEARNING TRACKS

Develop the following six courses.

Every course must have:

- Course title.
- Course description.
- Target audience.
- Entry requirements.
- Learning objectives.
- Expected duration.
- Modules.
- Detailed lessons.
- Practical demonstrations.
- Hands-on exercises.
- Module knowledge checks.
- Assignments.
- Final capstone project.
- Final assessment.
- Completion criteria.

Each course should contain at least four modules and three lessons per module.

This gives a minimum of 12 detailed lessons per course and 72 lessons across the six courses.

Do not create empty lesson pages or placeholder text such as "Content coming soon."

Write actual learner-facing course material.

