# PART 3: CONNECT EVERY COURSE TO THE DIGITAL SKILLS QUIZ

This is one of the most important technical requirements.

The learning tracks must not be independent of the quiz.

Create a shared learning-objective mapping system.

Each quiz question should be linked to:

- Category ID.
- Learning objective ID.
- Related course ID.
- Related module ID.
- Related lesson ID.
- Difficulty level.
- Question topic.

Example:

Category: AI & Emerging Technology

Question topic: Prompt Engineering

Learning objective: AI-PE-02

Course: AI Literacy and AI Product Building

Module: Module 2 – Prompt Engineering and AI Tools

Lesson: Lesson 2.2 – The Structure of an Effective Prompt

When a participant answers the question incorrectly, the result should identify Lesson 2.2 as a recommended learning destination.

### Required mapping logic

1. Inspect all existing questions in every category.
2. Identify the knowledge area each question tests.
3. Assign each question to a learning objective.
4. Map the learning objective to a course module and lesson.
5. Verify that the lesson actually teaches the tested knowledge.
6. Identify questions without an appropriate lesson.
7. Create or improve lesson content to close those gaps.

Do not simply assign lessons based on matching keywords.

The lesson must genuinely teach the concept or skill being assessed.

### Important rule

Every active quiz question must have at least one valid learning-objective mapping and at least one corresponding lesson.

Create an administrator-facing question-to-course coverage report.

The report should show:

- Total active questions.
- Questions mapped to learning objectives.
- Questions mapped to lessons.
- Unmapped questions.
- Courses with incomplete lesson coverage.

Do not report 100% coverage unless it has been verified.

