# PART 9: SECURITY AND FIREBASE COST OPTIMISATION

Security must be built into the implementation.

- Require authentication for private learning progress.
- Participants can only read and update their own progress.
- Administrators must have verified server-side roles or custom claims.
- Do not rely on hidden frontend buttons or routes for security.
- Protect administrator course-management operations.
- Protect quiz answers and official assessment scoring.
- Validate assessment submissions on a trusted backend where appropriate.
- Validate lesson completion and course completion rules.
- Prevent participants from editing their own official scores or granting themselves completion status.
- Validate project submissions and uploaded files.
- Do not place service-account keys or private API credentials in frontend code.

### Cost optimisation

- Load course lists efficiently.
- Load lessons only when needed.
- Avoid continuous Firestore listeners where not necessary.
- Avoid polling.
- Avoid unnecessary writes for every click.
- Save progress at sensible milestones.
- Use pagination for large admin reports.
- Use summary documents or trusted aggregation for analytics.
- Avoid duplicate course and question reads.

Do not introduce expensive infrastructure without a clear requirement.

